BEA’s developer portal, organized into four major tools:
---
1. Interactive Tables
These are the point‑and‑click interfaces you’ve already been exploring.
You can:
• Build custom GDP, industry, regional, or international tables
• Export to CSV, Excel, or PDF
• Generate charts
• Share links
Useful when:
• You want to explore data manually
• You’re deciding which dataset to automate later
• You need a quick snapshot for analysis
---
2. BEA API
This is the real power tool.
You can:
• Pull GDP, PCE, industry, regional, and international data
• Retrieve JSON or XML
• Automate updates
• Integrate into Python, R, JavaScript, or your dashboard backend
This is the piece that aligns with your goals:
• Data analytics training
• Building your intelligence dashboard
• Automating economic indicators
---
3. Open‑Source Tools (GitHub)
This links directly to the us‑bea GitHub organization you opened earlier.
You get:
• Python package (beaapi)
• R package (bea.R)
• Tools for regional aggregation
• Reproducible research notebooks
• Visualization guides
These are ideal for:
• Learning API workflows
• Building repeatable pipelines
• Integrating BEA data into VS Code projects
• Practicing Python + data engineering
---
4. News Release Feed (RSS)
This is for:
• Automated monitoring
• Triggering alerts
• Pulling new economic releases into your dashboard
If you want your dashboard to feel like a Bloomberg terminal, this is how you do it.